{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01PkUvPfjiN6s3VNHoyyDZth","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the project context and determine what to build next.\n\n## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils is an experiment in specification-driven development using classic Unix utilities as a test bed. They derive formal specifications from C source code, generate Go implementations from those specs using an AI coding agent, and verify parity against reference binaries through differential testing.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline: extract → specify → synthesize → verify. Key components:\n- `cmd/` - Go implementations of each utility\n- `pkg/testutils/` - Differential testing harness\n- `pkg/sys/` - Syscall abstractions (Darwin/Linux)\n\n\n- `pkg/format/` - Output formatting\n- `magefiles/` - Build targets\n\n**Current State**: Specifications are complete for ts, wc, cat, sponge, ls, and du with use cases and test suites written for all planned releases, but no implementations have been started yet.\n\n**Current Release**: rel01.0 is in progress with the ts utility as the first use case.\n\nLooking at the dependency chain, ts only needs pkg/testutils as a prerequisite—no pkg/sys or pkg/format dependencies. The implementation order should be pkg/testutils first (the differential testing harness), then cmd/ts, then its tests. Since I can only pick one task this batch and libraries must come before their consumers, I need to start with implementing pkg/testutils.\n\nNow I'm reviewing what testutils actually requires: a test case structure, binary execution with timeouts and working directory support, output comparison and reporting with normalization hooks, and file-state comparison for utilities like sponge and cp. That's substantial scope. The guidelines say to split implementation from tests into separate tasks, and each task needs to anchor to specific PRD requirements. But I'm constrained to just one task this batch, so I need to decide whether to implement testutils or defer and pick something else.\n\nLooking at the naming convention for Go packages, the primary source file should be named after the exported type, not the package name itself.\n\nI'm thinking through what should go into this implementation task. The DiffTest struct, Normalize type, RunDiffTests function, and comparison logic can all fit within the 250-350 line budget, so I'll structure this as a single cohesive implementation covering R1 through R5 of the PRD. Looking at the acceptance criteria, I need to ensure the implementation handles file expectations with proper divergence detection, timeout scenarios, and passes linting checks. Since I can only create one task and there's a clear dependency chain, the pkg/testutils implementation should come first—it has no dependencies and everything else builds on it. Let me map out the requirements and draft the task description. iffTest struct and Normalize type\n- R2.1-R2.5 → Binary execution logic\n- R3.1-R3.6 → Comparison and reporting\n- R4.1-R4.3 → Normalization hooks including TimestampNormalizer\n- R5.1-R5.2 → File-state comparison\n\nDesign decisions from the PRD and architecture:\n- Use testing.T for integration with go test\n- Use context.WithTimeout for configurable timeout (10s default)\n- Use t.Run for named subtests\n- TimestampNormalizer uses regexp to replace common strftime patterns\n\nI need to map the five requirement groups to task requirements. R1 covers the DiffTest struct with Args, Stdin, Env, ExitCode, and Normalize fields. R2 handles running both Go and reference binaries with identical inputs while capturing output and exit codes with configurable timeout and working directory. R3 implements the comparison logic that normalizes then does byte-for-byte comparison of stdout, stderr, and exit code, reporting any divergence as named subtests. R4 adds the normalization hook mechanism with per-test and composable normalizers, including the built-in TimestampNormalizer.\n\nFor the file structure, I'm planning two files: difftest.go will contain the DiffTest struct, Normalize function type, RunDiffTests entry point, execution logic, and comparison logic. normalizers.go will hold TimestampNormalizer and ComposeNormalizers. The implementation should be around 250-350 lines total.\n\nSince pkg/testutils only needs standard library packages like os/exec and testing, there's no need to modify go.mod. Now I'm finalizing the task title to include the requirement ID as specified: \"pkg/testutils: DiffTest struct, RunDiffTests harness, and TimestampNormalizer (prd001-testutils R1-R5)\". I'll document the required reading as docs/specs/product-requirements/prd001-testutils.yaml and write out the full task description. (the PRD for this component)\n- docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (for component description and project structure)\n- docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel01.0.yaml (to understand how tests will use this harness)\n\nFor files:\n- pkg/testutils/difftest.go - create - DiffTest struct, Normalize type, RunDiffTests, execution, comparison, reporting\n- pkg/testutils/normalizers.go - create - TimestampNormalizer and ComposeNormalizers\n\nRequirements (mapping to PRD):\n- R1: Define DiffTest struct with Args ([]string), Stdin ([]byte), Env ([]string), ExitCode (int), Normalize ([]Normalize), and FileExpectations fields per prd001-testutils R1.1-R1.4\n- R2: Implement binary execution that invokes both the Go binary and GNU reference binary with identical args, stdin, and env; capture stdout, stderr, and exit code independently with configurable timeout (default 10s) and optional working directory\n- R3: Implement comparison that applies Normalize functions to both outputs before byte-for-byte comparison of stdout, stderr, and exit code; report divergence with args, stdin (truncated to 256 bytes), both stdouts, both stderrs, and both exit codes; run each DiffTest as a named subtest\n- R4: Implement normalization hooks with per-DiffTest Normalize field as a slice of functions applied in order, plus a built-in TimestampNormalizer that replaces common timestamp patterns with a fixed value\n- R5: Implement file-state comparison for utilities whose output is a file, allowing DiffTest to specify expected file paths and content with byte-for-byte comparison and divergence reporting\n- R6: Export RunDiffTests as the single entry point\n\nDesign decisions:\n- D1: Primary source file is difftest.go (per ARCHITECTURE.yaml naming convention)\n- D2: Normalize is defined as a function type that transforms byte slices\n\n, with DiffTest.Normalize as a slice for composing multiple normalizers\n- D3: Binary execution uses os/exec.CommandContext with configurable timeouts\n- D4: RunDiffTests iterates over tests using t.Run for subtest isolation\n- D5: File-state comparison uses a FileExpectation field containing path and expected content, evaluated after both binaries complete\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- AC1: pkg/testutils compiles cleanly with `go build ./pkg/testutils/...`\n- AC2: RunDiffTests is exported and accepts the testing.T instance, binary paths, and test slice\n- AC3: DiffTest struct includes all required fields from the specification\n- AC4: TimestampNormalizer is exported and replaces strftime-formatted timestamps with a placeholder\n- AC5: ComposeNormalizers combines multiple Normalize functions into a single applied sequence\n- AC6: golangci-lint passes without warnings on pkg/testutils/\n\nI'm reconsidering whether all of these are truly checkable acceptance criteria—some feel more like implementation details than user-facing requirements. I need to add a Name field to DiffTest to support the named subtest requirement from R3.6, even though it wasn't explicitly mentioned in R1. Let me revise the acceptance criteria to make this concrete and ensure the struct definition includes all necessary fields for the test harness. I need to wrap up the DiffTest struct definition and move forward with writing the YAML specification. Since this is a greenfield implementation with no existing code, I'll create the necessary files from scratch rather than modifying existing ones. is a map or slice structure to hold the file paths and expected content, then both binaries write to separate temp directories and we compare the specified files against expectations. The PRD doesn't nail down the exact struct field names or types, so I'll keep the requirement description general and let the implementation handle those details.\n\nNow I'm mapping out the actual task: I need to create the DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests harness in pkg/testutils, along with a TimestampNormalizer, pulling from the PRD, architecture docs, and test suite specs to understand how this gets consumed downstream. The main files are difftest.go for the core logic and normalizers.go for the normalization strategies. I need to implement the binary execution logic that runs both the Go binary under test and the GNU reference binary with the same inputs, captures their outputs independently with a configurable timeout, and handles optional working directories. Then I'll add comparison logic that normalizes both outputs before checking stdout, stderr, and exit codes for divergences. I need to handle file-state comparison for utilities that write to files instead of stdout, allowing DiffTest to specify expected file paths and content, then compare them byte-for-byte using the same divergence reporting format. Then I'm exporting RunDiffTests as the single public entry point that a cmd/ package can call from a test function with a predefined slice of DiffTest cases.\n\nThe source file should be named difftest.go after the primary exported type rather than testutils.go. Normalize is a function type that takes and returns a byte slice, and DiffTest.Normalize holds a slice of these for composition—when empty or nil, no normalization happens. For binary execution, I'm using os/exec.CommandContext with a configurable timeout via context.WithTimeout, ensuring timeouts fail the test with a clear message rather than hanging. RunDiffTests will iterate through the test cases...\n\n...calling t.Run with each test's name to isolate subtests so failures are individually identifiable. This task is implementation only—tests for the package are handled separately per project convention.\n\nThe acceptance criteria cover the exported RunDiffTests function signature, the DiffTest struct with its required fields including Name, Args, Stdin, Env, ExitCode, Normalize, WorkDir, and file expectations. I also need to ensure TimestampNormalizer is exported to replace strftime patterns with a placeholder, ComposeNormalizers combines multiple normalizers in sequence, and the code passes golangci-lint checks. Let me write this out now.\n\nActually, I should verify the counts match the requirements. I have 6 requirements and 6 acceptance criteria, which fits the 5-8 range. The 5 design decisions also fall within the 3-5 target. For file scope, I'm touching 2 files which is reasonable even though the constraint mentions 5-7 as a target—that's more of an upper bound for larger tasks. This focused library implementation is appropriately scoped.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":71816,"cache_read_input_tokens":15594,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":71816},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2256056c-047e-4a69-a139-46519e93a92f","uuid":"baa84baf-a6c0-4eab-913d-995bfa320d6f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01PkUvPfjiN6s3VNHoyyDZth","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Looking at the project context, I need to analyze the state and determine the next task.\n\n**Project Summary:**\n- go-unix-utils is a specification-driven pipeline: extract specs from C source → generate Go implementations → verify via differential testing against GNU reference binaries\n- Current release: rel01.0 (in_progress) — first utility `ts` (timestamp stdin lines)\n- All specs are written; no code has been implemented yet\n- Dependencies: ts needs pkg/testutils (the differential testing harness), which has no dependencies of its own\n\n**Priority Analysis:**\nThe earliest incomplete release is rel01.0 (ts). Per the dependency map, ts requires only pkg/testutils. The canonical order is: libraries before consumers, implementation before tests. Therefore, the first task is implementing pkg/testutils — the shared differential testing harness that every utility depends on.\n\nLet me write the task to the output file."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":71816,"cache_read_input_tokens":15594,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":71816},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2256056c-047e-4a69-a139-46519e93a92f","uuid":"956b1938-61c1-4744-977f-671d6cee91e7"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01PkUvPfjiN6s3VNHoyyDZth","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Vw1Uy8bucAcG6nexUHUtQk","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/petardjukic/2025-objectives/go-unix-utils/.cobbler/measure-20260224-223122.yaml","content":"- index: 0\n  title: \"pkg/testutils: Implement DiffTest struct, RunDiffTests harness, and TimestampNormalizer (prd001-testutils R1-R5)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd001-testutils.yaml (complete PRD for this component -- all requirements R1-R5 and acceptance criteria AC1-AC6)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/testutils component description, project structure, and design decisions)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel01.0.yaml (how cmd/ts tests will consume RunDiffTests and TimestampNormalizer)\n      - go.mod (module path and existing dependencies)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/testutils/difftest.go\n        action: create\n        note: DiffTest struct, Normalize type, RunDiffTests entry point, binary execution, comparison, and divergence reporting logic\n      - path: pkg/testutils/normalizers.go\n        action: create\n        note: TimestampNormalizer and ComposeNormalizers functions\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: |\n          Define a DiffTest struct with fields: Name (string, used for t.Run subtest name),\n          Args ([]string), Stdin ([]byte, nil means immediate EOF per prd001 R1.2), Env\n          ([]string, nil means inherit test process environment per prd001 R1.3), ExitCode\n          (int, expected exit code), Normalize ([]Normalize, applied in order before comparison;\n          nil or empty means no normalization per prd001 R1.4), WorkDir (string, optional working\n          directory; empty means use a per-test temp directory per prd001 R2.5), and a file\n          expectation field for utilities that write output files instead of stdout (per prd001\n          R5.1). Define Normalize as type Normalize func([]byte) []byte. Per prd001-testutils\n          R1.1-R1.4.\n      - id: R2\n        text: |\n          Implement binary execution that accepts two binary paths (Go binary under test and GNU\n          reference binary), invokes both with identical Args, Stdin, and Env from the DiffTest,\n          captures stdout, stderr, and exit code from each independently, imposes a configurable\n          timeout (default 10 seconds) using context.WithTimeout, supports an optional WorkDir\n          (creating a per-test temp directory when not specified), and produces no output to the\n          test process stdout or stderr during a passing test run. Per prd001-testutils R2.1-R2.5.\n      - id: R3\n        text: |\n          Implement comparison logic that applies the DiffTest Normalize function slice (in order)\n          to both binaries' stdout and stderr before comparison, compares normalized stdout\n          byte-for-byte (any difference is a test failure), compares normalized stderr byte-for-byte\n          (any difference is a test failure), compares exit codes exactly (any difference is a test\n          failure), and reports divergence with: the DiffTest Args, Stdin content (truncated to 256\n          bytes if longer), reference binary stdout, Go binary stdout, reference stderr, Go stderr,\n          and both exit codes. Each DiffTest runs as a named subtest via t.Run(test.Name, ...) so\n          individual failures are identifiable in go test output. Per prd001-testutils R3.1-R3.6.\n      - id: R4\n        text: |\n          Implement a built-in TimestampNormalizer that replaces common strftime timestamp patterns\n          (e.g., \"Feb 19 12:34:56\" for \"%b %d %H:%M:%S\", ISO-8601 datetime prefixes) with a fixed\n          placeholder string so that ts differential tests pass despite wall-clock differences\n          between the Go and reference binary runs. Implement a ComposeNormalizers function that\n          accepts a variadic or slice of Normalize functions and returns a single Normalize function\n          that applies them in order. Per prd001-testutils R4.1-R4.3 and AC3.\n      - id: R5\n        text: |\n          Implement file-state comparison for utilities whose primary output is a file rather than\n          stdout (sponge, cp, mv). The DiffTest file expectation field allows specifying file paths\n          whose content should be compared after both binaries exit. Compare file content byte-for-byte\n          and report divergence in the same format as stdout divergence (showing both contents and\n          the triggering args). Per prd001-testutils R5.1-R5.2 and AC4.\n      - id: R6\n        text: |\n          Export RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary string, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest) as\n          the single public entry point. A cmd/ package defines a []DiffTest slice and calls\n          RunDiffTests from a standard TestXxx function with no other setup required. Per\n          prd001-testutils AC1.\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: |\n          Primary source file is difftest.go, named after the primary exported type DiffTest.\n          The file must not be named testutils.go. Per project naming convention in\n          ARCHITECTURE.yaml: \"Go packages must name the primary source file after the primary\n          exported type, not the package name.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: |\n          Normalize is defined as type Normalize func([]byte) []byte. DiffTest.Normalize is\n          []Normalize (a slice for composition per prd001-testutils R4.3). When nil or empty,\n          no normalization is applied (per prd001-testutils R1.4).\n      - id: D3\n        text: |\n          Binary execution uses os/exec.CommandContext with context.WithTimeout for the\n          configurable timeout (default 10 seconds). A test that exceeds the timeout fails\n          with a clear timeout message rather than hanging the test run. Per prd001-testutils\n          R2.3 and AC5.\n      - id: D4\n        text: |\n          RunDiffTests iterates the []DiffTest slice, calling t.Run(test.Name, func(t\n          *testing.T){...}) for subtest isolation so individual test case failures are\n          identifiable in go test output. Per prd001-testutils R3.6.\n      - id: D5\n        text: |\n          This task produces implementation only -- no test files. Tests for pkg/testutils\n          are a separate task. Do not create any _test.go files.\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build ./pkg/testutils/... compiles with no errors.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: |\n          RunDiffTests is exported with signature func(t *testing.T, goBinary string,\n          refBinary string, tests []DiffTest).\n      - id: AC3\n        text: |\n          DiffTest struct has all required fields: Name (string), Args ([]string), Stdin\n          ([]byte), Env ([]string), ExitCode (int), Normalize ([]Normalize), WorkDir (string),\n          and a file expectation field for post-execution file content comparison.\n      - id: AC4\n        text: |\n          TimestampNormalizer is exported and replaces strftime-formatted timestamp patterns\n          (e.g., \"Feb 19 12:34:56\") with a fixed placeholder string.\n      - id: AC5\n        text: |\n          ComposeNormalizers is exported and combines a slice of Normalize functions into a\n          single Normalize function that applies them in order.\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"golangci-lint runs clean on all files in pkg/testutils/ with no warnings.\"\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":71816,"cache_read_input_tokens":15594,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":71816},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2256056c-047e-4a69-a139-46519e93a92f","uuid":"d2ec0350-82e1-4b7a-bbc3-72d91029fc63"}
